From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:14:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher add new items from the first screen

An item the launcher adds by itself (a newly installed application, a
pinned shortcut or a pinned widget) skipped the first screen and went
to the second screen or a new one. This product's first screen holds
nothing, so exclude no screen from the search: it begins at the first
screen, which the space finder counts even while it is empty, and goes
on through the later screens in order. A new screen is added when no
candidate screen can accommodate the item's span. Items already on the
second screen stay put.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java | 5 +++--
 .../launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTaskTest.kt       | 3 +--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java
index 1d511852d1e3e11f68c2bbd5a1a2ac2b1ba1c616..733a9082f311c748d9289932b13e820fa8d82f56 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java
@@ -16,7 +16,6 @@
 package com.android.launcher3.model.tasks;
 
 import static com.android.launcher3.LauncherSettings.Favorites.ITEM_TYPE_APPLICATION;
-import static com.android.launcher3.WorkspaceLayoutManager.FIRST_SCREEN_ID;
 import static com.android.launcher3.WorkspaceLayoutManager.TAG;
 
 import android.content.Context;
@@ -78,7 +77,9 @@ public class AddWorkspaceItemsTask implements ModelUpdateTask {
         }
 
         final ArrayList<ItemInfo> addedItemsFinal = new ArrayList<>();
-        final IntSet excludedScreens = IntSet.wrap(FIRST_SCREEN_ID);
+        // No screen is excluded: the search starts at the first screen, which is always part of
+        // it, even while it holds nothing, and goes on through the later screens in order.
+        final IntSet excludedScreens = new IntSet();
         final Context context = taskController.getContext();
 
         synchronized (dataModel) {
